Emacsvox News -- History Of User-Visible Changes

Maintained by Emacsvox Contributors.

* Emacsvox Unreleased --- Current User-Visible Changes

Released notes are preserved in [[file:NEWS-2026.9.5][NEWS for Emacsvox 2026.9.5]].

** Interruptible Notmuch refresh and EAT history feedback

Refreshing the selected Notmuch search buffer queues its completion count on
the primary speech stream. Navigation interrupts it, and it no longer speaks
over the selected message through the notification stream. Refreshes that
finish in another buffer retain generic notification feedback.

Opening a Notmuch thread now selects its newest open, matching unread
message. When none is unread, it keeps Notmuch's initial selection.
Reading a sender line after a folded quote no longer goes silent when Emacs
leaves point in the preceding hidden text.

EAT line-mode history navigation speaks the recalled command without also
announcing the history-item counter or input-restored message. Those messages
remain visible in the echo area; unrelated messages and errors are preserved.

** Native Windows installation

The native Windows x64 installer can download a verified complete GNU Emacs
with =-DownloadEmacs=. Use =-Offline= with a prepared archive cache to install
without network access. Existing explicit Emacs selections are preserved.

Development Windows Setup builds add a per-user wizard, Start menu and
optional desktop shortcuts, repair and uninstall. Uninstall preserves the
user's profile, logs and downloaded voices by default, with separate optional
cleanup choices and an explanation of any retained shared voices. The wizard
names the bundled versions, uses Emacsvox Windows for shortcuts, and explains
launch and uninstall when installation finishes.

** Welcome screen

An idle first startup offers speech testing, rate and output settings, voices,
the tutorial and manual. The startup toggle is saved per Emacs profile.
Reopen the screen with C-h W or M-x emacsvox-welcome.

** Agent Shell

Agent Shell 0.78.1 support keeps brackets editable at the persistent prompt
while the agent works. Viewport submission feedback distinguishes queueing
from steering, including the override command and unsupported-steering
fallback. Full header speech includes the optional cumulative cost indicator.
Reading a busy live prompt briefly says "Agent busy" or "Waiting for
permission", without repeating how input will be submitted.

Rendered table borders are omitted from response and line speech, preventing
decorative box-drawing characters from forcing an Eloquence-to-eSpeak switch.
Literal box-drawing characters now receive Unicode names through the existing
emoji and symbol naming settings.
Control-Meta-Left and Control-Meta-Right move between table columns; plain Left
and Right retain character navigation.
Outside editable input, t and T jump to the next and previous rendered table.
Both keys insert normally in live prompts and the viewport editor.
